   "source": [
    "================================================================\n",
    "B. WHAT GITHUB IS, AND HOW THIS CLASS CHECKS WORK\n",
    "================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "Git is a tool on your laptop. It saves snapshots called commits.\n",
    "GitHub is a website (github.com) that hosts Git repositories. The lecturer\n",
    "grades what is on GitHub, not a USB stick, not email, not a screenshot.\n",
    "\n",
    "From Week 1, 3 kinds of work all live in ONE class repository:\n",
    "\n",
    "  Classwork  (studio activity)  → folder 01 Classwork\n",
    "  Assignment (take-home)        → folder 02 Assignment\n",
    "  Quiz       (in-class answers) → folder 03 Quiz\n",
    "  Midterm    (Week 7)           → folder 04 Midterm\n",
    "  Final      (Weeks 13–14)      → folder 05 Final\n",
    "\n",
    "The repository name is exactly: Class-1-Student-Output\n",
    "\n",
    "TREE (do not rename folders; spaces and numbers are part of the name)\n",
    "\n",
    "——————————————————————————————————-\n",
    "Class-1-Student-Output/\n",
    "  README.md\n",
    "  _roster.md                       ← lecturer lists every Student Folder\n",
    "  01 Classwork/\n",
    "    M26W0000_Horiguchi/                  ← one folder per student\n",
    "      C01_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "      C02_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "      ...\n",
    "    M26W0001_Chen/\n",
    "      C01_M26W0001_Chen.ipynb\n",
    "  02 Assignment/\n",
    "    M26W0000_Horiguchi/\n",
    "      A01_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "      A02_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "      ...\n",
    "    M26W0001_Chen/\n",
    "      A01_M26W0001_Chen.ipynb\n",
    "  03 Quiz/\n",
    "    M26W0000_Horiguchi/\n",
    "      Q01_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "  04 Midterm/\n",
    "    M26W0000_Horiguchi/\n",
    "      M_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "  05 Final/\n",
    "    M26W0000_Horiguchi/\n",
    "      F_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "    \n",
    "Student Folder name = StudentNo_LastName  (example: M26W0000_Horiguchi)\n",
    "  • No spaces, just underscore. No first name. Use the number on your school ID.\n",
    "  • The same folder name is reused under 01, 02, 03, 04, and 05.\n",
    "\n",
    "THIS WEEK (1) you submit (example student M26W0000_Horiguchi):\n",
    "  01 Classwork/M26W0000_Horiguchi/C01_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "\n",
    "Naming rules\n",
    "  Classwork:   C{week two digits}_StudentNo_LastName.ipynb\n",
    "  Assignment:  A{assignment two digits}_StudentNo_LastName.ipynb\n",
    "  Quiz:        Q{week two digits}_StudentNo_LastName.ipynb\n",
    "  Midterm:     M_StudentNo_LastName.ipynb\n",
    "  Final:       F_StudentNo_LastName.ipynb  (plus css/ and images/ beside it)\n",
    "\n",
    "================================================================\n",
    "STUDENT — access YOUR folder and submit without touching others\n",
    "================================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Create a GitHub account at github.com/signup with your school email.\n",
    "   Professional username (not xXgamerXx). Enable 2FA.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Tell the lecturer your username so they can add you as a collaborator\n",
    "   and so your name is spelled correctly on _roster.md.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Accept the email invite from GitHub.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Clone ONCE (not every week):\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Find YOUR Student Folder. Example: 01 Classwork/M26W0000_Horiguchi\n",
    "   If you cannot see your folder, stop and ask. Do not create a second\n",
    "   spelling (Horiguchi vs horiguchi). GitHub folder names are case-sensitive.\n",
    "\n",
    "6. Right-click YOUR folder → New File → type the exact name for this week.\n",
    "   Example classwork: C01_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb\n",
    "\n",
    "7. Open with Live Server. Validate. Then submit:\n",
    "   Activity Bar → Source Control.\n",
    "   Changed files appear. Confirm they sit under YOUR folder only.\n",
    "   If you see someone else's path, right-click → Discard Changes. Do not\n",
    "   stage it.\n",
    "   Message examples:\n",
    "     \"C01 classwork: tag detective\"\n",
    "     \"A01 assignment: profile page\"\n",
    "     \"Q01 quiz\"\n",
    "     \"midterm: night desk page\"\n",
    "     \"final: harbor radio site\"\n",
    "   Click Commit (stage all IF the list is only your files).\n",
    "   Click Sync / Publish Branch.\n",
    "\n",
    "8. Refresh github.com/Class-1-Student-Output. Click through 01 Classwork → your folder.\n",
    "   The file must be there before you leave studio (classwork) or before\n",
    "   the deadline (assignment).\n",
    "\n",
    "HOW YOU AVOID OVERWRITING OTHER STUDENTS\n",
    "  • Never open another student's folder \"to help\". Talk, do not type.\n",
    "  • Never rename, move, or delete folders. The lecturer owns the tree.\n",
    "  • Never copy your file into 01 Classwork/ as a loose file. It must sit\n",
    "    inside your Student Folder.\n",
    "  • Never create a second clone on the Desktop and copy files by hand\n",
    "    unless you know which clone Source Control is watching (the green\n",
    "    branch name on the Status Bar).\n",
    "  • If Git says \"conflict\": do not click random buttons. Call the lecturer.\n",
    "    Conflicts happen when two people edited the SAME file. That should\n",
    "    not occur if everyone stays in their own folder.\n",
    "  • Forking is not used in this class. One shared repo. Collaborators\n",
    "    push to the same main branch, different paths.\n",
    "\n",
    "THIS WEEK'S DROPBOX PATH (copy this into your README if you keep notes)\n",
    "  01 Classwork/M26W0000_Horiguchi/C01_M26W0000_Horiguchi.ipynb (a perfect example)\n",
    "\n",
    "The instructor grades the commit on GitHub. A perfect file that lives only\n",
    "on your laptop is not submitted."
   ]
  }
 ],
